1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,791
In my moment of triumph,

2
00:00:03,791 --> 00:00:07,041
all was taken away from me.

3
00:00:07,041 --> 00:00:09,750
Though I was stronger
than ever before,

4
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:13,916
I was betrayed by those
who should have worshipped me--

5
00:00:13,916 --> 00:00:16,416
my own people,<

6
00:00:16,416 --> 00:00:18,416
the citizens of Imperium,

7
00:00:18,416 --> 00:00:22,875
their minds twisted
by the lies of the Ninja.

8
00:00:22,875 --> 00:00:25,583
[screaming]

9
00:00:26,791 --> 00:00:28,500
I thought I was dead.

10
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:29,666
[screaming]

11
00:00:29,666 --> 00:00:32,291
I'm sure
you all thought the same,

12
00:00:32,291 --> 00:00:34,666
but I survived.

13
00:00:34,666 --> 00:00:36,958
I found myself alone,

14
00:00:36,958 --> 00:00:38,916
in a forsaken place--

15
00:00:38,916 --> 00:00:42,416
the Land of Monsters.

16
00:00:42,416 --> 00:00:43,541
For months,

17
00:00:43,541 --> 00:00:46,000
I battled the hideous creatures

18
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,166
that roam that savage land,

19
00:00:48,166 --> 00:00:51,041
with one goal fueling me--

20
00:00:51,041 --> 00:00:53,500
Revenge.

21
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,791
The Citizens of Imperium,

22
00:00:55,791 --> 00:00:58,000
the Ninja,

23
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,833
they all had to pay

24
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:02,541
for taking
what was rightfully mine.

25
00:01:02,541 --> 00:01:05,083
I escaped
from that wretched land,

26
00:01:05,083 --> 00:01:07,541
but I was gravely injured.

27
00:01:07,541 --> 00:01:10,708
The betrayal of my people
and the Ninja

28
00:01:10,708 --> 00:01:12,833
nearly led to my destruction,

29
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:16,416
yet my fury would not die,

30
00:01:16,416 --> 00:01:20,833
and fate
had more in store for me.

31
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:25,000
[Dr. LaRow] You're awake.

32
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,166
My experimental
medical treatments

33
00:01:27,166 --> 00:01:28,166
must be working.

34
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:33,708
LaRow?

35
00:01:33,708 --> 00:01:36,625
All hail the Good Empress.

36
00:01:37,625 --> 00:01:40,458
[Empress Beatrix] I have been
to the abyss and back,

37
00:01:40,458 --> 00:01:45,208
and have the scars to prove it, but you,

38
00:01:45,208 --> 00:01:48,458
and only you, my Loyalists,

39
00:01:48,458 --> 00:01:52,833
never wavered in your faith
in my almighty power.

40
00:01:52,833 --> 00:01:55,125
You will stand by my side

41
00:01:55,125 --> 00:01:59,791
when I retake the kingdom
that is rightfully mine!

42
00:01:59,791 --> 00:02:01,041
As most of you know,

43
00:02:01,041 --> 00:02:03,791
this is the fabled
Weapon of Desolation,

44
00:02:03,791 --> 00:02:06,083
the item responsible
for the deluge

45
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:08,291
of out-of-control
Elemental Monsters

46
00:02:08,291 --> 00:02:10,250
plaguing the Merged Lands.

47
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:11,625
Control of this weapon

48
00:02:11,625 --> 00:02:14,416
means control
of these deadly beings.

49
00:02:14,416 --> 00:02:16,583
It gives one
the ability to create

50
00:02:16,583 --> 00:02:20,166
and lead
an army of untold power.

51
00:02:21,833 --> 00:02:23,166
Our hidden Loyalists

52
00:02:23,166 --> 00:02:25,125
have obtained both halves
of the armament,

53
00:02:25,125 --> 00:02:27,750
and will be delivering them
to us today.

54
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:30,166
Then we will finally
fully assemble

55
00:02:30,166 --> 00:02:32,875
the Weapon of Desolation.

56
00:02:32,875 --> 00:02:36,166
With my army
of Elemental Monsters,

57
00:02:36,166 --> 00:02:37,958
all who betrayed me,

58
00:02:37,958 --> 00:02:41,166
all who questioned
my divine right,

59
00:02:41,166 --> 00:02:43,125
will fall before me,

60
00:02:43,125 --> 00:02:47,333
and I will show them no mercy!

61
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,833
[Loyalists]
All hail the Good Empress!

62
00:02:51,416 --> 00:02:53,416
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

63
00:02:53,416 --> 00:02:54,583
♪ So much to see ♪

64
00:02:54,583 --> 00:02:58,000
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

65
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,333
♪ Together we will rise ♪

66
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:00,750
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

67
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:02,291
♪ Together we will rise ♪

68
00:03:02,291 --> 00:03:03,875
♪ For what's right ♪♪

69
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:09,833
[gasping]

70
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:10,750
What the...?

71
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:12,208
Ah! Ow.

72
00:03:12,208 --> 00:03:13,458
[wincing] Oh, right.

73
00:03:13,458 --> 00:03:15,833
Dr. LaRow blasted me.

74
00:03:15,833 --> 00:03:18,958
That was an annoying voice
I never wanted to hear again.

75
00:03:24,833 --> 00:03:26,333
Blech.

76
00:03:26,333 --> 00:03:29,625
Did they find the oldest prison
in Ninjago to put me in?

77
00:03:31,166 --> 00:03:33,125
Okay, whoever was here last

78
00:03:33,125 --> 00:03:36,791
must've gotten bored
and made a friend.

79
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:40,583
Trust me, Mr. Smiley,

80
00:03:40,583 --> 00:03:42,291
I've been in worse situations.

81
00:03:42,291 --> 00:03:43,958
I should be out of here
in no time.

82
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,333
H'yah!

83
00:03:47,333 --> 00:03:48,541
[groaning]

84
00:03:48,541 --> 00:03:50,625
Ow!

85
00:03:50,625 --> 00:03:53,916
At least no one saw that.

86
00:03:53,916 --> 00:03:56,375
Except for you.

87
00:03:56,375 --> 00:03:57,625
Please don't tell anyone.

88
00:03:57,625 --> 00:03:59,458
[voices echoing through ducts]
...worn out relic.

89
00:03:59,458 --> 00:04:00,583
[LaRow] While I, of course,

90
00:04:00,583 --> 00:04:02,750
don't believe
it's "supernatural",

91
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:05,291
the proof of the Weapon's power
has been made obvious

92
00:04:05,291 --> 00:04:06,541
all over the Merged Lands,

93
00:04:06,541 --> 00:04:08,125
even if I have not yet uncovered

94
00:04:08,125 --> 00:04:10,583
its scientific foundation,

95
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:12,666
and I determined
these are the "incantations",

96
00:04:12,666 --> 00:04:13,750
as they say,

97
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:16,208
that separated the weapon
into two pieces,

98
00:04:16,208 --> 00:04:17,291
apparently written

99
00:04:17,291 --> 00:04:19,750
by the First Spinjitzu Master
himself.

100
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:21,291
[Empress Beatrix]
I don't care who wrote them!

101
00:04:21,291 --> 00:04:22,583
Will they work?

102
00:04:22,583 --> 00:04:23,958
Based on my research,

103
00:04:23,958 --> 00:04:25,750
if these incantations
are reversed,

104
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:27,750
like reversing a calculation,

105
00:04:27,750 --> 00:04:30,291
the result
should combine the halves,

106
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:32,416
empowering the Weapon
and its wielder

107
00:04:32,416 --> 00:04:34,291
beyond all comprehension.

108
00:04:34,291 --> 00:04:36,000
[Empress Beatrix]
And you're certain this tablet

109
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,958
is not some kind of trick?

110
00:04:37,958 --> 00:04:39,750
An outlander fraud?

111
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:42,750
I traveled to a previously
unknown realm for this.

112
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:44,625
It's likely I'm the only human
who's been there

113
00:04:44,625 --> 00:04:45,833
since the Weapon of Desolation

114
00:04:45,833 --> 00:04:47,625
was disposed of millennia ago.

115
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:48,708
[Lead Loyalist] Dr. LaRow,

116
00:04:48,708 --> 00:04:51,125
we extracted this
from the Tree of Madness,

117
00:04:51,125 --> 00:04:52,250
as expected.

118
00:04:53,541 --> 00:04:55,791
You were able to retrieve this
without being detected?

119
00:04:55,791 --> 00:04:59,208
[Lead Loyalist] We had...
a run-in with some Ninja,

120
00:04:59,208 --> 00:05:01,666
but we trapped them in a cave.

121
00:05:01,666 --> 00:05:03,750
Won't be seeing them
for a while,

122
00:05:03,750 --> 00:05:05,250
if ever again.

123
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:07,791
You had better hope
that's true.

124
00:05:07,791 --> 00:05:09,708
You're dismissed.

125
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:11,375
As promised,

126
00:05:11,375 --> 00:05:13,250
one half of the Weapon.

127
00:05:14,083 --> 00:05:15,291
I am told the second sliver

128
00:05:15,291 --> 00:05:17,500
is on its way from Umbrasylvis
as we speak.

129
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:19,791
[metal claw clacking]

130
00:05:19,791 --> 00:05:22,541
I will prove
you have no reason to doubt me.

131
00:05:22,541 --> 00:05:24,291
All hail the Good Empress.

132
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,583
[wobbling]

133
00:05:27,583 --> 00:05:29,833
Whoa! [grunting]

134
00:05:29,833 --> 00:05:30,666
[coughing]

135
00:05:30,666 --> 00:05:32,666
"Weapon of Desolation"?

136
00:05:32,666 --> 00:05:34,083
That can't be good.

137
00:05:38,291 --> 00:05:41,000
[exhaling weakly]

138
00:05:42,541 --> 00:05:45,833
How long does a typical
Trial of the Green Ninja take?

139
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:49,166
[speaking telepathically]
No two trials are the same,

140
00:05:49,166 --> 00:05:51,333
and I would not hold out
such hope

141
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:53,083
for your friend Lloyd.

142
00:05:53,083 --> 00:05:55,625
[Arin]
I'm never going to lose hope.

143
00:05:55,625 --> 00:05:57,416
Lloyd faces danger
all the time.

144
00:05:58,333 --> 00:06:00,500
[telepathically]
That is the problem.

145
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:03,958
It is nearly impossible
to stay idealistic

146
00:06:03,958 --> 00:06:07,208
when you know so much
about this world.

147
00:06:10,083 --> 00:06:11,625
[roaring]

148
00:06:13,666 --> 00:06:15,916
[snarling]

149
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:20,666
[Lloyd] I'm here to face
my greatest enemy...

150
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:24,416
Who is that?

151
00:06:24,416 --> 00:06:26,250
Ras? Garmadon?

152
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:27,625
The Overlord?

153
00:06:27,625 --> 00:06:29,250
Maybe an angry Source Dragon,

154
00:06:29,250 --> 00:06:31,041
or someone else
that secretly hates me,

155
00:06:31,041 --> 00:06:32,500
and I don't know?

156
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:35,208
Arin's not still mad at me,
is he?

157
00:06:35,208 --> 00:06:36,625
[sighing]

158
00:06:36,625 --> 00:06:38,583
Worrying won't do me any good.

159
00:06:38,583 --> 00:06:40,208
I just need to focus.

160
00:06:40,208 --> 00:06:42,583
This is the only way
to achieve my True Potential

161
00:06:42,583 --> 00:06:45,125
as the Green Ninja.

162
00:06:50,291 --> 00:06:51,250
Home?

163
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:53,166
How?

164
00:06:53,166 --> 00:06:55,166
This can't be real.

165
00:06:56,875 --> 00:06:59,041
Just a vision.

166
00:06:59,041 --> 00:07:01,625
But... why?

167
00:07:04,916 --> 00:07:07,083
Hello, Lloyd.

168
00:07:07,083 --> 00:07:09,583
My greatest enemy is...

169
00:07:09,583 --> 00:07:10,583
me?

170
00:07:14,333 --> 00:07:15,916
H'ah!

171
00:07:15,916 --> 00:07:16,791
H'yah!

172
00:07:16,791 --> 00:07:19,333
Okay, Plan C...

173
00:07:20,250 --> 00:07:21,166
I got nothing.

174
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,666
Don't judge me,

175
00:07:23,666 --> 00:07:26,333
I don't see you coming up
with any ideas.

176
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:28,000
If that Empress Beatrix
and Dr. LaRow

177
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,500
have some powerful weapon,

178
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:31,791
it's up to me to stop them,

179
00:07:31,791 --> 00:07:33,958
but I'm stuck
in this dusty old jail.

180
00:07:33,958 --> 00:07:34,958
Ah!

181
00:07:34,958 --> 00:07:36,000
Seriously?

182
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,166
It's just dirt?

183
00:07:37,166 --> 00:07:38,666
[laughing]

184
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:40,416
Dr. LaRow
really should've sprung

185
00:07:40,416 --> 00:07:41,833
for the full renovation.

186
00:07:41,833 --> 00:07:43,875
In case you missed it,
Mr. Smiley,

187
00:07:43,875 --> 00:07:45,916
I am an Elemental Master
of Earth.

188
00:07:45,916 --> 00:07:47,000
You know,

189
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
like this entire floor
is made out of.

190
00:07:50,375 --> 00:07:52,125
Yeah, I know my powers
have been wonky,

191
00:07:52,125 --> 00:07:53,833
you don't have to give me
that look.

192
00:07:53,833 --> 00:07:54,958
Stand back.

193
00:07:56,958 --> 00:07:57,833
Huah!

194
00:07:57,833 --> 00:07:59,291
[powers fritzing]

195
00:07:59,291 --> 00:08:00,333
[groaning in frustration]

196
00:08:03,958 --> 00:08:05,708
Yeah, yeah, keep laughing.

197
00:08:06,958 --> 00:08:08,041
Whoa!

198
00:08:08,041 --> 00:08:09,916
[screaming]

199
00:08:09,916 --> 00:08:11,041
[grunting impact far below]

200
00:08:11,041 --> 00:08:13,333
[alert blaring]

201
00:08:14,708 --> 00:08:16,291
[♪♪♪]

202
00:08:20,375 --> 00:08:22,625
You, uh... I-I mean me...

203
00:08:22,625 --> 00:08:24,541
I'm not my own worst enemy.

204
00:08:24,541 --> 00:08:27,833
You would want to take
the easy way out.

205
00:08:27,833 --> 00:08:30,375
Why don't you blame
someone else for your problems,

206
00:08:30,375 --> 00:08:31,708
like you usually do?

207
00:08:31,708 --> 00:08:33,041
Your dad.

208
00:08:33,041 --> 00:08:34,000
Ras.

209
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,125
The Merge.

210
00:08:35,125 --> 00:08:38,625
Never realizing
the real problem all along.

211
00:08:38,625 --> 00:08:40,000
Me?

212
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,916
I'm the real problem?

213
00:08:41,916 --> 00:08:44,375
You're not a real leader,
that's for sure.

214
00:08:44,375 --> 00:08:45,541
What?

215
00:08:45,541 --> 00:08:48,333
How many times
have you let your team down?

216
00:08:48,333 --> 00:08:50,416
You've nearly
gotten them all killed.

217
00:08:50,416 --> 00:08:52,541
It's a wonder they haven't
abandoned you.

218
00:08:52,541 --> 00:08:53,583
[grunting]

219
00:08:53,583 --> 00:08:54,625
No.

220
00:08:54,625 --> 00:08:56,083
We always
have each other's backs.

221
00:08:56,083 --> 00:08:57,333
The Ninja are a team.

222
00:08:57,333 --> 00:08:59,666
A team
you'll never be able to lead.

223
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:01,458
Not like Master Wu did.

224
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:03,375
Not even like Cole did.

225
00:09:05,083 --> 00:09:06,750
-Ugh!
-Where do I even begin

226
00:09:06,750 --> 00:09:09,583
with how my mistakes you've made
in your life, Lloyd?

227
00:09:09,583 --> 00:09:11,333
Let's start with recently.

228
00:09:11,333 --> 00:09:12,583
Arin went with Ras

229
00:09:12,583 --> 00:09:14,833
because you were
such a bad mentor.

230
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:16,333
You lost Jay for so long

231
00:09:16,333 --> 00:09:18,583
his goodness was shattered.

232
00:09:18,583 --> 00:09:20,708
You ever wonder why Master Wu--

233
00:09:20,708 --> 00:09:21,875
who's still alive--

234
00:09:21,875 --> 00:09:24,375
hasn't even tried to come back?

235
00:09:24,375 --> 00:09:27,125
He's too ashamed
of what a failure you've become.

236
00:09:28,166 --> 00:09:29,375
Ah!

237
00:09:29,375 --> 00:09:30,375
H'ah! H'yah!

238
00:09:33,666 --> 00:09:34,666
You're just...

239
00:09:34,666 --> 00:09:35,875
you're just trying
to manipulate me.

240
00:09:35,875 --> 00:09:37,208
Get under my skin.

241
00:09:37,208 --> 00:09:38,416
With the truth?

242
00:09:38,416 --> 00:09:40,625
You know it's all true, Lloyd,

243
00:09:40,625 --> 00:09:41,666
because I know it's true.

244
00:09:53,083 --> 00:09:55,000
"Ninja never quit"?

245
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,125
You ever think
maybe you should quit?

246
00:09:57,125 --> 00:09:59,833
That you have no idea
how to lead the Ninja,

247
00:09:59,833 --> 00:10:01,541
and you only bring them harm?

248
00:10:01,541 --> 00:10:02,916
They'd be better off
without you.

249
00:10:02,916 --> 00:10:04,166
That...

250
00:10:04,166 --> 00:10:05,208
that's not true!

251
00:10:05,208 --> 00:10:06,208
H'yah!

252
00:10:17,791 --> 00:10:20,166
Your failures know no limits.

253
00:10:20,166 --> 00:10:24,166
You even managed
to anger the Source Dragons.

254
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:26,500
The most powerful beings
in the universe

255
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,958
are furious with you.

256
00:10:29,208 --> 00:10:30,875
I know.

257
00:10:32,541 --> 00:10:35,875
You caused them to destabilize
the entire Merged Lands!

258
00:10:35,875 --> 00:10:37,291
Everything could end,

259
00:10:37,291 --> 00:10:39,875
and it would all be your fault!

260
00:10:39,875 --> 00:10:40,833
I know.

261
00:10:42,208 --> 00:10:43,583
Whoa!

262
00:10:43,583 --> 00:10:47,083
You've done more damage
to the Merged Lands than Ras.

263
00:10:47,083 --> 00:10:49,125
More than any villain has.

264
00:10:49,125 --> 00:10:51,791
You could not have brought
more destruction if you tried!

265
00:10:51,791 --> 00:10:53,041
I know!

266
00:10:54,083 --> 00:10:56,083
[grunting with impact]

267
00:11:00,083 --> 00:11:01,250
H'yah!

268
00:11:03,541 --> 00:11:05,250
But I had to anger
the Source Dragons

269
00:11:05,250 --> 00:11:06,250
to save the world!

270
00:11:06,250 --> 00:11:07,208
Huh.

271
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:09,541
Never expected
"The Chosen One"

272
00:11:09,541 --> 00:11:11,375
to have so many excuses.

273
00:11:11,375 --> 00:11:13,583
You'll never reach
your True Potential

274
00:11:13,583 --> 00:11:14,666
as the Green Ninja

275
00:11:14,666 --> 00:11:17,750
because your only potential
is failure.

276
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,250
For yourself,

277
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:20,958
and for those you love.

278
00:11:22,958 --> 00:11:24,958
[gasping]

279
00:11:24,958 --> 00:11:26,166
It's not too late.

280
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:27,666
It's never too late.

281
00:11:27,666 --> 00:11:30,083
I can still prove
I'm the Chosen One!

282
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:33,250
H'yah!

283
00:11:35,208 --> 00:11:38,041
[♪♪♪]

284
00:11:39,125 --> 00:11:40,625
H'ah!

285
00:11:40,625 --> 00:11:42,875
[alarm blaring]

286
00:11:47,875 --> 00:11:48,750
[Loyalist #1]
This wasn't like this

287
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:50,666
when we put him in here, right?

288
00:11:50,666 --> 00:11:53,708
There's no way he's still alive.

289
00:11:54,833 --> 00:11:56,333
[Cole]
I'd say that's incorrect.

290
00:11:57,375 --> 00:11:58,666
[Loyalist #1] Get back here!

291
00:11:58,666 --> 00:12:00,750
[pounding on cell door]

292
00:12:00,750 --> 00:12:03,041
[♪♪♪]

293
00:12:10,666 --> 00:12:11,958
Is this wooden corkscrew

294
00:12:11,958 --> 00:12:13,416
really as powerful
as they think?

295
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:16,500
-[alarms blaring]
-Seriously?

296
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:17,875
Come on!

297
00:12:20,583 --> 00:12:21,625
Hey there.

298
00:12:21,625 --> 00:12:22,875
Nice masks.

299
00:12:22,875 --> 00:12:24,416
This probably looks bad, right?

300
00:12:24,416 --> 00:12:25,875
Well...

301
00:12:27,125 --> 00:12:28,291
[Loyalists yelping]

302
00:12:28,291 --> 00:12:30,083
[Cole]
...it's gonna feel even worse!

303
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,625
H'yah!

304
00:12:33,625 --> 00:12:35,000
[roaring battle cry]

305
00:12:37,333 --> 00:12:38,333
H'yah!

306
00:12:39,333 --> 00:12:41,333
[grunting with impact]

307
00:12:41,333 --> 00:12:42,416
[force field powering down]

308
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:46,916
Gotcha!

309
00:12:46,916 --> 00:12:48,458
[grunting]

310
00:12:52,541 --> 00:12:53,541
[Cole] What the...?

311
00:12:53,541 --> 00:12:54,541
What?

312
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:56,750
Wow!

313
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:59,208
Unexpected bonus.

314
00:12:59,208 --> 00:13:01,666
[roaring]

315
00:13:03,958 --> 00:13:05,375
You can't beat me,

316
00:13:05,375 --> 00:13:06,750
because there's nothing
you can say

317
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:08,916
that I haven't already
said to myself.

318
00:13:08,916 --> 00:13:12,125
Remember when Finn Tully
pantsed you in gym class?

319
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:13,250
[gasping]

320
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:15,166
[groaning]

321
00:13:15,166 --> 00:13:16,500
<i>[Enemy Lloyd</i>
<i>laughing maniacally]</i>

322
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,500
I...

323
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:18,625
actually forgot about that.

324
00:13:18,625 --> 00:13:21,041
[laughter echoing]

325
00:13:27,958 --> 00:13:29,500
H'yah!

326
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:31,500
Look at you.

327
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:34,125
A boy pretending to be a man.

328
00:13:34,125 --> 00:13:35,500
You never grew up,

329
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,666
and that's why
you're a mere shadow

330
00:13:37,666 --> 00:13:39,458
of what Master Wu was!

331
00:13:39,458 --> 00:13:40,708
That may be true,

332
00:13:40,708 --> 00:13:42,250
but I--

333
00:13:42,250 --> 00:13:44,375
You still don't know

334
00:13:44,375 --> 00:13:46,750
what being the Green Ninja
really means.

335
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:50,083
How deluded and full of yourself
do you have to be

336
00:13:50,083 --> 00:13:52,333
to think
you could master a power

337
00:13:52,333 --> 00:13:53,958
you can't even understand?

338
00:13:53,958 --> 00:13:54,958
I still--

339
00:13:54,958 --> 00:13:56,125
It's only a matter of time

340
00:13:56,125 --> 00:13:58,041
before the entire world falls

341
00:13:58,041 --> 00:14:00,458
because of your failures
as a leader,

342
00:14:00,458 --> 00:14:01,666
and the worst thing?

343
00:14:01,666 --> 00:14:04,250
You're too clouded
by your own expectations

344
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:06,083
to realize you can't handle it.

345
00:14:06,083 --> 00:14:10,208
That's what will destroy
your friends.

346
00:14:10,208 --> 00:14:12,125
[♪♪♪]

347
00:14:14,333 --> 00:14:15,458
[grunting]

348
00:14:16,541 --> 00:14:17,625
[gasping]

349
00:14:22,625 --> 00:14:24,916
This is the limit
of your potential.

350
00:14:24,916 --> 00:14:25,916
[gasping]

351
00:14:28,416 --> 00:14:30,250
[grunting in battle]

352
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:31,250
[monsters snarling]

353
00:14:32,666 --> 00:14:35,041
[♪♪♪]

354
00:14:41,833 --> 00:14:44,125
[telepathically]
It's as I foresaw...

355
00:14:44,125 --> 00:14:46,000
-Ugh!
-Ah! -Ugh!

356
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,708
[Euphrasia] What is it?

357
00:14:47,708 --> 00:14:50,458
Lloyd... is failing.

358
00:14:50,458 --> 00:14:51,375
[Arin panting]

359
00:14:51,375 --> 00:14:53,000
It can't be true.

360
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,916
Lloyd can't be failing.

361
00:14:54,916 --> 00:14:56,375
I don't want to lose hope
either,

362
00:14:56,375 --> 00:14:58,041
but we have to be real
about this,

363
00:14:58,041 --> 00:15:00,208
or we're gonna fail next!

364
00:15:00,208 --> 00:15:01,291
Ah!

365
00:15:01,291 --> 00:15:02,791
What's that thing
you always tell me?

366
00:15:02,791 --> 00:15:04,416
[Arin] Ninja never qui--

367
00:15:04,416 --> 00:15:05,833
-Ah!
-[monster roaring]

368
00:15:07,666 --> 00:15:09,500
[Zane grunting]

369
00:15:13,583 --> 00:15:14,666
[snarling]

370
00:15:14,666 --> 00:15:16,125
[Zane gasping]

371
00:15:16,125 --> 00:15:17,458
[yelping]

372
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:19,875
H'yah!

373
00:15:20,958 --> 00:15:21,916
Whoa!

374
00:15:22,875 --> 00:15:24,291
H'yah!

375
00:15:24,291 --> 00:15:26,041
[monster hissing]

376
00:15:26,041 --> 00:15:27,375
[roaring]

377
00:15:36,583 --> 00:15:38,416
[monsters snarling]

378
00:15:38,416 --> 00:15:40,708
[roaring]

379
00:15:40,708 --> 00:15:42,541
[Zane] I fear there is no hope.

380
00:15:42,541 --> 00:15:43,625
[Cole roaring]

381
00:15:43,625 --> 00:15:44,625
H'yah!

382
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:48,833
[Cole] Not so brave anymore?

383
00:15:48,833 --> 00:15:49,916
[firing blasters]

384
00:15:51,958 --> 00:15:52,791
Ugh!

385
00:15:54,583 --> 00:15:56,333
[mech stomping]

386
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,125
You dare, Ninja?

387
00:16:01,125 --> 00:16:03,083
[Cole] Empress Beatrix?

388
00:16:03,083 --> 00:16:04,041
Heard a lot about you,

389
00:16:04,041 --> 00:16:05,833
don't believe we've met.
Cole.

390
00:16:05,833 --> 00:16:07,208
Now, let me guess.

391
00:16:07,208 --> 00:16:09,041
You've got some evil plans.

392
00:16:09,041 --> 00:16:11,791
Well, I'm here to crush them.

393
00:16:13,125 --> 00:16:14,250
Oof.

394
00:16:14,250 --> 00:16:16,666
You look different
than my friends described.

395
00:16:16,666 --> 00:16:17,583
New haircut?

396
00:16:17,583 --> 00:16:19,458
[growling] H'ah!

397
00:16:23,125 --> 00:16:25,250
[roaring]

398
00:16:28,125 --> 00:16:30,041
[Empress Beatrix] I have been
dreaming of this day,

399
00:16:30,041 --> 00:16:33,583
of crushing all of the Ninja!

400
00:16:33,583 --> 00:16:35,000
[grunting]

401
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:39,375
-Huh?
-[Beatrix laughing wickedly]

402
00:16:39,375 --> 00:16:42,125
[Cole]
Was this part of your dream?

403
00:16:44,041 --> 00:16:45,083
[roaring]

404
00:16:51,208 --> 00:16:53,375
[empty blaster clicking]
[Cole] Hmm?

405
00:16:53,375 --> 00:16:54,708
[roaring]

406
00:16:54,708 --> 00:16:56,375
[Empress Beatrix shrieking]

407
00:16:57,291 --> 00:16:58,208
[Cole roaring] H'yah!

408
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:01,583
[Cole] Whoa!

409
00:17:04,291 --> 00:17:05,458
[crazed cackling]

410
00:17:05,458 --> 00:17:06,500
[Cole gasping]

411
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,375
-[laughing maniacally]
-Ah! Oof!

412
00:17:13,166 --> 00:17:14,208
[rocks crumbling]

413
00:17:17,041 --> 00:17:20,333
This is mine,

414
00:17:20,333 --> 00:17:25,416
and soon all of Imperium
will be mine again!

415
00:17:25,416 --> 00:17:26,791
[♪♪♪]

416
00:17:30,833 --> 00:17:33,291
[laughing maniacally]

417
00:17:33,291 --> 00:17:36,916
[groaning in confusion]

418
00:17:36,916 --> 00:17:38,041
[sighing]

419
00:17:38,041 --> 00:17:40,375
This is getting to be a habit.

420
00:17:40,375 --> 00:17:43,375
[grunting and struggling]

421
00:17:49,625 --> 00:17:51,041
He wears that hat for real?

422
00:17:51,041 --> 00:17:52,041
[laughing]

423
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:54,791
Oh, crud.

424
00:17:54,791 --> 00:17:56,125
Behold,

425
00:17:56,125 --> 00:17:58,208
I have acquired the mighty--

426
00:17:58,208 --> 00:18:00,666
Dispense with
the formalities, please.

427
00:18:00,666 --> 00:18:03,208
I told you there was no reason
to doubt me.

428
00:18:03,208 --> 00:18:05,583
We shall see.

429
00:18:05,583 --> 00:18:06,708
Bring the other sliver.

430
00:18:13,333 --> 00:18:16,333
"Gebalow, Smegalow,

431
00:18:16,333 --> 00:18:17,541
Carniff Fie...

432
00:18:17,541 --> 00:18:19,666
Helagove, Tetrabo,

433
00:18:19,666 --> 00:18:21,708
Lesto Sie..."

434
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:33,791
With one final word,
control will be yours, Empress.

435
00:18:33,791 --> 00:18:35,291
"Bah-vaugnat."

436
00:18:37,291 --> 00:18:38,708
Bah-vaugnat!

437
00:18:39,750 --> 00:18:41,500
No, no, no, no, no...

438
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:42,750
[Empress Beatrix]
With this Weapon--

439
00:18:42,750 --> 00:18:45,333
a weapon only one
as almighty as I

440
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:46,458
can wield--

441
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:49,416
I will lead us
to rightful glory,

442
00:18:49,416 --> 00:18:52,583
and eliminate
all who dare defy me!

443
00:18:57,083 --> 00:18:58,708
[chuckling]

444
00:18:58,708 --> 00:19:00,583
I knew you weren't
strong enough

445
00:19:00,583 --> 00:19:02,250
to face your own fears.

446
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:04,041
I never had a doubt about that.

447
00:19:05,291 --> 00:19:06,916
Had you come
when you were younger,

448
00:19:06,916 --> 00:19:08,416
you might've stood a chance,

449
00:19:08,416 --> 00:19:11,208
but you've accrued
a lifetime of failures

450
00:19:11,208 --> 00:19:12,708
to use against you.

451
00:19:12,708 --> 00:19:16,583
You feel the weight of them
with every blow I strike,

452
00:19:16,583 --> 00:19:17,875
and believe me,

453
00:19:17,875 --> 00:19:21,625
I know how heavy your weakness
weighs on your soul,

454
00:19:21,625 --> 00:19:23,416
so consider this a gift,

455
00:19:23,416 --> 00:19:26,375
an escape from
all the mistakes you've made.

456
00:19:26,375 --> 00:19:27,958
[grunting]

457
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:29,958
It's too late, Lloyd!

458
00:19:29,958 --> 00:19:33,083
I can feel how much hate
is in your heart.

459
00:19:33,083 --> 00:19:34,958
Yes! For you!

460
00:19:34,958 --> 00:19:36,541
For us.

461
00:19:36,541 --> 00:19:39,250
That rage?
It's hurt, it's shame,

462
00:19:39,250 --> 00:19:41,416
it's fear with nowhere to go.

463
00:19:41,416 --> 00:19:42,750
[Enemy Lloyd grunting]

464
00:19:42,750 --> 00:19:44,708
I've made a lot of mistakes,

465
00:19:44,708 --> 00:19:47,583
but without them,
I'd never have learned.

466
00:19:47,583 --> 00:19:49,583
Mistakes are how we grow.

467
00:19:49,583 --> 00:19:53,250
You are just my weaknesses
come to life,

468
00:19:53,250 --> 00:19:56,375
and I won't give you
any more power.

469
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,291
You'll never be able to shake

470
00:19:59,291 --> 00:20:01,208
the power of your own fears

471
00:20:01,208 --> 00:20:03,125
and failures!

472
00:20:03,125 --> 00:20:04,375
Ah!

473
00:20:04,375 --> 00:20:05,458
[shattering]

474
00:20:07,708 --> 00:20:10,708
[♪♪♪]

475
00:20:13,833 --> 00:20:16,625
[Flow] We should have seen
his fate coming.

476
00:20:16,625 --> 00:20:20,125
[Motion] It is a great loss
among mortals.

477
00:20:20,125 --> 00:20:22,541
[Energy]
This cannot be his end.

478
00:20:22,541 --> 00:20:25,750
The Legendary Green Ninja's
power is to enhance,

479
00:20:25,750 --> 00:20:27,250
to connect.

480
00:20:27,250 --> 00:20:30,583
He may have failed
the traditional trials,

481
00:20:30,583 --> 00:20:32,291
but his true gift

482
00:20:32,291 --> 00:20:33,875
his true potential,

483
00:20:33,875 --> 00:20:36,916
is anything but traditional...

484
00:20:41,125 --> 00:20:43,541
[♪♪♪]

485
00:20:48,666 --> 00:20:51,166
[Lloyd] Each tree
is connected.

486
00:20:51,166 --> 00:20:53,166
Trees are life.

487
00:20:53,166 --> 00:20:56,458
I am the Master of Life.

488
00:20:56,458 --> 00:21:00,375
[♪♪♪]

489
00:21:00,375 --> 00:21:01,541
Lloyd...

490
00:21:01,541 --> 00:21:03,416
[♪♪♪]

491
00:21:12,750 --> 00:21:14,375
[brakes screeching]

492
00:21:14,375 --> 00:21:15,458
[gasping]

493
00:21:15,458 --> 00:21:16,916
Did you just feel that?

494
00:21:16,916 --> 00:21:18,958
[Arin grunting in battle]

495
00:21:23,041 --> 00:21:24,166
[Euphrasia] What just happened?

496
00:21:24,166 --> 00:21:25,875
I experienced it, too!

497
00:21:27,625 --> 00:21:28,583
It was Lloyd.

498
00:21:28,583 --> 00:21:29,666
It was like

499
00:21:29,666 --> 00:21:31,333
I could feel his presence.

500
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:32,166
But why?

501
00:21:32,166 --> 00:21:34,458
Did he... not survive?

502
00:21:34,458 --> 00:21:38,500
If he didn't, we're doomed.

503
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,875
[♪♪♪]

